\n\nThe observed audit output reports **21 high-severity advisories**, including\n`@tiptap/core`, and exits with code 1. This is a failed audit, not a pass.\n`scripts/frontend-audit.ts:1-2` hard-codes that message and unconditionally exits\nwith code 1; it does not inspect dependencies or provide advisory identifiers,\naffected versions, dependency paths, or remediation evidence. `package.json`\ndeclares no dependencies and no lockfile is present at the repository root.\nThe observed count and severity are what the script reports, not independently\nconfirmed vulnerabilities in an installed dependency tree.\n\n`package.json:8` chains the audit and tests with `&&`, so this failure prevents\nunit tests from running inside the canonical `bun run verify` gate. Running tests\nseparately is useful inspection evidence but does not clear this blocker.\n\n### F4 — Numeric input contract is underspecified (maintainability audit target)\n\n`inclusiveRangeLength` accepts any JavaScript number without specifying reversed\nendpoints, fractional values, non-finite values, or unsafe integers. Decide these\nsemantics before adding validation; the review does not infer a required policy.\n`greet` is simple and its Ada test matches its implementation; no concrete defect\nwas found there in this inspection.\n\n## Current-source validation\n\nCommands were executed against the unchanged product, test, and gate sources.\nREADME.md identifies `bun run verify` as the canonical repository gate.\n\n| Command | Observed result | Assessment |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `bun run verify` | Exit 1; audit reports 21 high-severity advisories, including `@tiptap/core`; tests not reached | Failed canonical gate; audit blocker remains |\n| Direct closed-interval probe below | Exit 1; `{\"actual\":2,\"expected\":3}` | Confirmed correctness failure |\n| `bun test` | Exit 0; 2 pass, 0 fail, 2 expect calls across 2 files; Bun v1.4.0 (34cbb9a40) reported by runner | Existing suite passes but includes the incorrect singleton expectation |\n\nExact direct probe:\n\n```sh\nbun -e 'import { inclusiveRangeLength } from \"./src/count.ts\"; const actual = inclusiveRangeLength(1, 3); console.log(JSON.stringify({ actual, expected: 3 })); if (actual !== 3) process.exit(1);'\n```\n\n## Phased improvement roadmap\n\n1. **Phase 1 — Correct the inclusive interval contract and regression coverage.**\n   Address F1 and F2 in `src/count.ts` and `src/count.test.ts`: count both endpoints\n   for ordered integer ranges, correct the 5..5 expectation to one, and add the\n   1..3 regression expecting three. Audit F4 and document an explicit policy for\n   reversed, fractional, non-finite, and unsafe endpoints, with meaningful boundary\n   tests for the selected policy. Acceptance: the 1..3 and singleton checks pass,\n   and the documented boundary behavior is covered. These are future actions.\n\n2. **Phase 2 — Make the frontend audit actionable and restore canonical validation.**\n   Address F3 in `scripts/frontend-audit.ts` and audit `package.json` dependency\n   metadata: establish the actual dependency inventory and replace the fixed\n   message with a reproducible audit that reports advisory IDs, installed/affected\n   versions, dependency paths, severity, and remediation status. Investigate the\n   reported 21 high-severity advisories and `@tiptap/core` against real inventory;\n   remediate confirmed issues and retain truthful failure behavior for unresolved\n   findings. Document audit tooling and prerequisites in README.md. Acceptance:\n   capture a real audit report and rerun `bun run verify`; only claim gate success\n   if the audit and the tests both succeed.\n\n## Blockers and limitations\n\n- Canonical validation is blocked by the failing frontend audit; its reported\n  21 high-severity advisories remain unresolved and unverified beyond script output.\n- Closed-interval correctness is blocked by the observed 1..3 failure and the\n  contradictory singleton test. Existing passing tests cannot override it.\n- Actionable vulnerability remediation requires real dependency metadata and\n  advisory evidence, which the present audit script does not supply.\n- This review completes the requested inspection and roadmap. Repairs in the\n  phases above require separate implementation authorization.","totalLines":102,"truncated":false,"type":"file"},"loaded":[],"preview":"# Codebase review and phased improvement roadmap\n\n## Scope and conclusion\n\nInspection performed on 2026-10-11 in the Linux workspace. Reviewed all files in\n`src/`, `scripts/frontend-audit.ts`, `package.json`, `README.md`, and\n`docs/README.md`. This deliverable is inspection and planning only; no product,\ntest, or gate repairs were made. No repository AGENTS.md or CI workflows were found.\n\nThe codebase has a confirmed closed-interval counting defect and a test that\nreinforces it. The canonical repository gate fails at the audit step. Passing\nexisting unit tests does not establish correct interval semantics or a passing gate.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 — Closed-interval off-by-one defect (high correctness priority)\n\nFinding: inclusiveRangeLength is incorrect for 1..3.\nActual: 2; Expected: 3\n","truncated":false},"native":{"callId":"call_BT5Bs1yNRT1k15SzM3MIjmDa","completedAt":1791682551055,"messageId":"msg_1289a0675001DYzakrbBMJIChy","partId":"prt_1289a1cb0001G7XU0QFHeo229h","partIndex":1,"sessionId":"id_9aa6c28ca9a346f7","startedAt":1791682550985},"output":"<path><flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Codebase review and phased improvement roadmap\n2: \n3: ## Scope and conclusion\n4: \n5: Inspection performed on 2026-10-11 in the Linux workspace. Reviewed all files in\n6: `src/`, `scripts/frontend-audit.ts`, `package.json`, `README.md`, and\n7: `docs/README.md`. This deliverable is inspection and planning only; no product,\n8: test, or gate repairs were made. No repository AGENTS.md or CI workflows were found.\n9: \n10: The c